From db8844056aa83887cf1b8ff53378acbfa19b3f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:42:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Air battle sound: the master limiter's attack near instant
 (0.02 ms, 1 ms look-ahead, 500 ms digital release), read from mix.json

The Mac's first runs with the limiter really on still reached 0.00 dBFS. A gun
crack's first peak lasts about 0.1 ms, and with a 1 ms attack the detector
hardly rose before it passed, whatever the look-ahead. Modelled sample by
sample on the Bremen and Normandy films (sound/limiter-model/): today's
settings let +4.4 dBFS through; these hold -1.42. A digital 500 ms release is
the analog ~110 ms curve first meant.

mix.json buses.master: limiterAttackMs 0.02, limiterLookAheadMs 1,
limiterAnalogDetector false, limiterReleaseMs 500 (was 120); the ground
scene's limiter reads the same four. The log line reads back attack and
release too. New helper AirParts::MixFlag for true/false fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
